# NOTE 05: JWT AUTHENTICATION, RBAC & QR SECURITY NOTES
## Complete Bit-by-Bit Study Guide & Security Examples for Zaika Restaurant Management System

================================================================================
1. ZAIKA'S 4-ROLE SECURITY ARCHITECTURE
================================================================================
Zaika serves four distinct user groups, each requiring tailored access control:
1. Customer (`customer`): Zero login or registration required. Authenticated purely by scanning a table's unique QR URL (`?table=T1&token=tok_t1_99a1`). Can browse the menu, place orders, track cooking timers, play the Spice Quiz, call a waiter, pay bills, and leave reviews.
2. Staff / Waiter (`staff`): Login required (email + password -> JWT token). Can view the Live Floor Map, confirm customer orders ("Send to Kitchen"), resolve Call Waiter alerts, and process table billing.
3. Kitchen Staff (`kitchen`): Login required (JWT token). Restricted strictly to the 3-Station Kitchen Display System (`Tandoor`, `Curry`, `Drinks`) to mark items `Cooking` -> `Ready`.
4. Owner / Admin (`owner`): Login required (JWT token). Full administrative access to Owner Analytics, Menu Management (Add/Edit/Delete dishes), Staff Account Creation, and SQLite Audit Logs.

