4. ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL (RBAC) ROUTE GUARDS
================================================================================
Using Python closures, we create a reusable `require_role([...])` dependency. Any FastAPI endpoint protected with `Depends(require_role(["owner"]))` automatically blocks unauthorized roles with a `403 Forbidden` status code before the function body even runs!

```python
def require_role(allowed_roles: List[str]):
    def role_checker(current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user)) -> User:
        if current_user.role not in allowed_roles:
            raise HTTPException(
                status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,
                detail=f"Access denied. Required role: {allowed_roles}, your role: '{current_user.role}'"
            )
        return current_user
    return role_checker
```

How Role Guards Protect Your Endpoints Across Routers:
```python
from fastapi import APIRouter

# Example 1: Owner-Only Menu Creation
@router.post("/api/menu", status_code=201)
def add_menu_item(
    payload: MenuItemCreate,
    db: Session = Depends(get_db),
    owner: User = Depends(require_role(["owner"]))
):
    # Only runs if JWT belongs to an active 'owner'
    ...

# Example 2: Staff OR Owner Can Confirm Orders to Kitchen
@router.patch("/api/orders/{order_id}/confirm")
def confirm_order_to_kitchen(
    order_id: int,
    db: Session = Depends(get_db),
