6. CUSTOMER QR TOKEN VERIFICATION (NO-LOGIN SECURITY)
================================================================================
Even though customers do not log in, each table (T1–T6) has a unique secret qr_token stored in restaurant_tables (e.g., tok_t1_99a1). When a customer scans the QR code on Table T1, Streamlit reads ?table=T1&token=tok_t1_99a1 and verifies it against this public endpoint so pranksters cannot place fake orders for Table T5 by guessing URLs.
```python
from backend.models import RestaurantTable
@router.get("/verify-qr")
def verify_table_qr(table: str, token: str, db: Session = Depends(get_db)):
record = db.query(RestaurantTable).filter(
RestaurantTable.table_number == table,
RestaurantTable.qr_token == token
).first()
if not record:
raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail="Invalid or expired Table QR Code")
return {
"valid": True,
"table_id": record.id,
"table_number": record.table_number,
"status": record.status,
"current_points": record.current_points
}
```

